phys={17:('I_27.html','27-2 mirror sign convention n=-1; plane-surface limit','Reflect point x=d across mirror x=0 to x=-d; separation2d=200cm. Exact plane geometry; published distances retained.'),43:('I_21.html','21-2 oscillator equation m*xddot=-kx','Assume falling block has zero horizontal speed, negligible spring impulse during collision, no damping afterward. Horizontal momentum gives v_new=v/2, omega_new=omega/sqrt(2). Hence A_new^2=x^2+v^2/(2omega^2)=(A^2+x^2)/2. It decreases away from a turning point and is unchanged at a turning point; phase matters, D. Vertical impact energy is dissipated, not assigned to horizontal oscillation.'),105:('I_21.html','21-1 pendulum as oscillator; own exact nonlinear pendulum derivation','For ideal point bob/massless inextensible string, theta_ddot=-(g/L)sin(theta). Set tau=t*sqrt(g/L): trajectory at fixed release angle is L-independent in tau, so T=sqrt(L/g)*F(theta0), mass-independent even at finite amplitude. Decreasing angle from horizontal increases angle from downward vertical, so increases rather than decreases finite-amplitude period. B alone decreases period.'),137:('I_49.html','49-1 Eqs49.5/49.6; both-end boundary discussion','Use the ordinary laboratory driven-string resonance convention with effectively nodal endpoints, small driver displacement, steady resonant modes. y=sin(kx) requires sin(kL)=0 so L=n*lambda/2. A explains missing resonance; speed fixed and lambda=v/f alone do not. This is conditional on that standard boundary convention, not a statement about free-end or arbitrary forced waves.'),42:('I_04.html','4-2/4-3 conservative energy and turning-point argument','Ideal conditions interpreted as spherical nonrotating Earth, drag-free tunnel, no energy loss. Along a diameter U(x)=U(-x), minimized at center. Release from rest at R has E=U(R), so speed nonzero at center, zero at -R, then acceleration reverses motion. No escape energy. Uniform density is unnecessary for oscillation; required only for exact sinusoidal motion.'),12:('I_39.html','39-4 molecular collision exchange; own canonical momentum derivation for liquid extension','In the classical thermal-equilibrium model H=sum p_i^2/(2M_i)+U(q), the canonical momentum factor exp[-p_i^2/(2M_i kT)] gives mean center-of-mass translational kinetic energy3kT/2 independent of molecular mass, including intermolecular U(q) in liquids. Collisions/interactions exchange energy. This does not equalize every molecule or rotational/vibrational internal energy. D is the intended mean translational-energy statement.')}
cp={167:('I_15.html','15-1 and15-4 own-frame principle','Steady inertial motion leaves own local clock/bodily measurements normal; distinguish observer-frame relativistic mass convention from rest mass. D.'),73:('','Sun facts; light/energy discussion plus radiation model','The interplanetary near-vacuum prevents conduction/convection as the textbook Sun-to-Earth heat-transfer mechanism. Energy arrives as electromagnetic radiation; ignore minor particle energy flux.'),30:('II_40.html','40-1 hydrostatic pressure relation before Eq40.1','At equal supported atmospheric pressure rho*g*h is fixed. Water is less dense than mercury, so taller column; ideal static column/vapor correction neglected.'),138:('','NIST uranium dating and age-of-Earth discussion','Radioactive minerals date early Earth; decay predates discovery, industry and medicine. D identifies primordial presence; no claim all current radionuclides existed then.'),65:('','NASA sonic-boom misconception paragraph','NASA explicitly distinguishes continuous supersonic-wave production from merely crossing Mach1. C; ground observer hears passage of wavefront, not continuous noise forever.'),200:('I_07.html','7-1 inverse-square law','For spherical central source F=GMm/r^2, circular radius constant, other listed noncircular conics vary r. Elliptical means noncircular ellipse in ordinary list taxonomy.'),90:('II_22.html','resistor I=V/R and22-6 series addition','Conventional fixed-voltage source and ordinary resistive lamps: Rtotal=sumRi increases when adding series lamp, I=V/Rtotal decreases. Not an ideal current-source circuit; textbook convention explicitly retained.'),48:('I_47.html','47-1 longitudinal-vs-transverse paragraph','Longitudinal means particle displacement parallel to propagation, A. Vietnamese propagation verb is awkward but stem/choices retain the longitudinal-vibration contrast.'),139:('','NASA types of eclipses opening solar-eclipse definition','Moon between Sun/Earth shadows Earth: solar eclipse. Day/night distractor does not change eclipse type.'),178:('I_04.html','4-2 lifting work and gravitational energy','Interpret work as work by hoist against gravity with equal initial/final kinetic energy, conventional lifting question. W=mgh=100*9.8*2=1960J, approximate2000J;4s affects power only. Net work by all forces would instead be change in K; that is not the textbook applied lifting-work meaning.'),189:('I_15.html','Eq15.6 and15-6 simultaneity','Read observer appears in standard textbook coordinate-measurement sense, measuring endpoints simultaneously in observer frame: Lparallel=L0/gamma and perpendicular lengths unchanged. No viewing direction/camera is specified, so no photographic/Terrell-shape prediction is inferred. All languages retain this same conventional interpretation.'),137:('','DLMF1.2(v) norm/scalar product; own construction','Choose perpendicular components (3,0),(0,4): magnitude5. Triangle inequality gives1<=R<=7 so0 and8 impossible. B.'),2:('I_27.html','27-2 water reciprocal index3/4 and Snell reference','For ordinary water index4/3, air approx1, Snell gives sin(theta_air)=(4/3)sin20deg=0.456<1. Transmitted ray exists; critical angle arcsin(3/4)=48.59deg. Partial reflection does not make total internal reflection true.'),230:('II_40.html','40-1 pressure gradient; own buoyancy integral','Integrate hydrostatic pressure over closed balloon surface: buoyancy=rho_water*g*V. Flexible gas balloon compresses under rising depth pressure, V decreases, buoyancy decreases. Conventional incompressible lake water and compliant gas balloon; attached rock weight is not buoyant-force growth.'),191:('','NASA free-fall acceleration','Once released hand force vanishes; only mg remains, so a=g downward independent of initial speed. A.'),49:('I_13.html','conservative work/potential definitions','DeltaU=-Wconservative. Quasistatic work against spring/electrical conservative force stores potential energy; motion itself is not its definition. Use same reference zero for comparisons.'),68:('','NASA Wave Behaviors reflection/absorption','Opaque material does not transmit incident beam; reflection or absorption into material energy explains choices. Ordinary passive nonfluorescent material model; absorbed energy can later be re-emitted.'),208:('I_49.html','49-1 second mode twice first frequency','Second harmonic is2f1 by definition; source string mode gives same ratio. B.'),98:('I_04.html','4-2 ideal reversible lifting machine; own work balance','Ideal lossless pulley at constant lifting speed:25N*1m=100N*h, h=.25m=25cm. A.'),135:('I_09.html','Eq9.9 Cartesian Newton equations','In ideal drag-free projectile motion Fx=0 so vx constant; vertical component changes under gravity. Ordinary textbook assumption, not a claim about real aerodynamic baseball motion.'),46:('II_17.html','17-4 transformer coupling plus own ideal energy balance','Ideal means no dissipative losses or accumulating average stored energy. Conservation over steady cycle gives Pout=Pin; voltage/current may transform inversely. Chinese unchanged is read relative to input comparison, C.'),127:('I_33.html','33-1 electric-vector transverse orientations','Polarization distinguishes orientation in transverse plane; longitudinal scalar-direction displacement lacks this freedom. Chinese broader term is disambiguated by wave/answer context.'),143:('II_40.html','40-1 p=p0+rho*g*depth','At fixed atmospheric pressure ordinary pond bottom pressure depends on rho,g,depth, not surface area. D. No claim p0 vanishes.'),106:('I_04.html','Eq4.6 kinetic energy','Fixed nonrelativistic mass: Knew/Kold=(3v/v)^2=9. None of numeric alternatives matches, including ambiguous three-times-greater distractor.'),111:('I_30.html','30-2 grating regularly spaced coherent sources','Regularly spaced wave contributions sum with phase differences; interference gives maxima/minima. Question multilingual meaning retained; old Vietnamese supporting constructive terminology needs replacement.'),102:('','CIAAW table Z8oxygen/Z10neon plus own nucleon count','Ne20 has10protons/10neutrons. Removing2each leaves Z8,A16, oxygen16. Treat as bookkeeping hypothetical, not assertion of spontaneous decay channel; old Vietnamese evidence atomic-number term requires correction.')}
